meta {
  name: News feed redirect
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/redirect/news-feed/:itemId?utm_source=opencti&utm_medium=newsfeed&utm_campaign=hub_resources&utm_content=other&platform_id=
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  itemId:
}

docs {
  Public endpoint, no auth required, rate limited per IP (60 requests per minute).

  itemId: id of a news feed item (UUID, not the Relay global id). Its type must have a destination builder,
  today only BLOG_POST, built from the document_id metadata (the blog post slug).

  Answers a 302 with Cache-Control: no-store:
  - to the destination built from the item type and metadata, e.g. https://www.filigran.io/blog/<slug>
    (only the utm_* query parameters are forwarded to filigran.io, platform_id never is)
  - to the hub root (/) for a malformed id, an unknown or deleted item, a type without a builder or invalid metadata.
    The response is identical in every case.

  Answers a 429 when the rate limit is exceeded.

  platform_id (optional, UUID) is only used as a label of the news_feed_redirect telemetry event.
  If the request carries a session cookie, the event also carries the user and the organization. The session is never
  created nor modified.
}
